(Q&A TRANSCRIPT) '
([Venture Capitalist] How big can FitBite get? Walk me through the market size for) '
(FitBite primarily targets **health-conscious students and yo.) '
(A: FitBite has the potential to become a large digital nutrition and wellness platform,) '
(starting with health-conscious students and young professionals in India.**TAM  Total) '
(Addressable Market:**India's broader digital health market is already substantial and is) '
(projected to grow rapidly. More specifically, India's wellness-app market generated) '
(approximately **$579 million in 2024** and is projected to reach **$1.44 billion by) '
(2030**, growing at 16.4% annually.**SAM  Serviceable Available Market:**FitBite can) '
(initially focus on the nutrition and personalized-health segment. India's diet and) '
(nutrition apps market generated about **$109 million in 2024** and is projected to reach) '
(**$257 million by 2030**, with a 15.3% CAGR. India's personalized nutrition market was) '
(estimated at **$213 million in 2025** and is projected to reach **$289 million by) '
(2030**.**SOM  Serviceable Obtainable Market:**Our initial goal is to capture a small) '
(share of this growing market by targeting digitally active students and young) '
(professionals in major Indian cities. If FitBite eventually reaches **1 million paying) '
(users at an average of Rs 150 per month**, that would represent approximately **Rs 180) '
(crore in annual subscription revenue**, before additional revenue from food partnerships) '
(and corporate wellness.India's young population provides a strong long-term customer) '
(base: people aged 1024 represented about **26% of India's population in 2025**.Our) '
(long-term vision is to expand from personalized meal recommendations into a broader) '
(**AI-powered nutrition and wellness platform**, creating multiple revenue streams beyond) '
(subscriptions.We're not building just another diet app. We're starting with personalized) '
(nutrition for India's young, health-conscious population, then expanding into a complete) '
(AI-powered wellness platform. Even capturing a small share of India's growing nutrition) '
(and wellness-app markets can create a significant business.) '
() '
([Founder] What will you ship in the next 90 days, and who does the work?) '
(A: Over the next 90 days, we will launch and validate the first working version of) '
(FitBite.**Days 130  Build the MVP*** Launch the core FitBite web/mobile experience.*) '
(Build user onboarding for goals, dietary preferences, allergies, budget, and lifestyle.*) '
(Develop the AI-powered personalized meal recommendation engine.* Create an initial) '
(database of meals and nutritional information.**Days 3160  Beta Launch*** Launch a beta) '
(version to approximately 200500 users.* Track engagement, meal-plan usage, retention,) '
(and user feedback.* Improve recommendation quality based on real user behavior.* Add) '
(grocery planning and basic progress tracking.**Days 6190  Validate & Grow*** Expand the) '
(beta to approximately 1,000 users.* Test the premium subscription model.* Begin) '
(partnerships with healthy food and grocery providers.* Measure conversion, retention,) '
(and customer acquisition costs.* Use the results to prepare for a larger public) '
(launch.**Who does the work:**The founding team will lead product development, AI/model) '
(integration, user research, and growth. We will use a small number of contractors or) '
(specialists where necessary for nutrition validation, UI/UX, and legal/compliance) '
(requirements.At the end of 90 days, our goal is to have a **working product, real users,) '
(measurable engagement data, and early evidence of willingness to pay**.) '
() '
([Customer] I'm part of "FitBite primarily targets **health-conscious students and yo".) '
(Why would I switch from what I use today to FitBite?) '
(A: Today, people rely on generic diet plans, social-media advice, calorie-tracking apps,) '
