([Venture Capitalist] What's your path to 10x scale, and what stops a big player from) '
(copying you?) '
(A: Our path to 10x scale is to expand FitBite from a personalized nutrition app into a) '
(broader AI-powered wellness platform.**First, we scale the core product** from students) '
(and young professionals to families, fitness users, and corporate wellness programs. We) '
(can expand through campus partnerships, fitness communities, influencers, and employer) '
(wellness programs rather than relying only on paid advertising.**Second, we expand) '
(geographically.** Once the model is validated in India, FitBite can adapt meal) '
(recommendations to different cuisines, budgets, and dietary preferences across other) '
(markets.**Third, we build additional revenue streams** through premium subscriptions,) '
(corporate wellness, grocery and healthy-food partnerships, and personalized nutrition) '
(services.A large company could copy individual features, but our advantage comes from) '
(the combination of **personalized user data, recommendation quality, user feedback) '
(loops, localized nutrition knowledge, and a trusted ecosystem of food and wellness) '
(partners**. The more users interact with FitBite, the better we can understand what) '
(recommendations are practical and effective for different lifestyles.Our goal is to make) '
(FitBite difficult to replacenot simply difficult to copy.) '
() '
([Founder] What's the biggest execution risk for FitBite and how will you handle it?) '
(A: Our biggest execution risk is **user retention and trust**. Many people try health) '
(and diet apps but stop using them when recommendations feel generic, unrealistic, or) '
(difficult to follow.We will address this by launching with a focused target audience and) '
