([Customer] Tell me about the last real person who felt this problem. What did they do?) '
(A: The last person we spoke to who experienced this problem was a young college student) '
(living away from home. She wanted to eat healthier but had a limited budget, a busy) '
(class schedule, and very little time or ability to cook.Her current solution was mostly) '
(to **eat whatever was available near college or order food online**, while occasionally) '
(searching Instagram and YouTube for healthy-diet advice. The problem was that these) '
(options were either convenient but unhealthy, or healthy but difficult to plan and) '
(maintain consistently.This isn't an isolated problem. Recent research involving 68 young) '
(adults across eight Indian cities found that young people identified **cost, easy) '
(availability of unhealthy food, limited cooking time, independent living, and peer) '
(influence** as major barriers to healthy eating.That's the gap FitBite is designed to) '
(solve: instead of asking a busy student to figure out nutrition on their own, FitBite) '
(gives them **a practical, personalized, and budget-conscious choice for what to eat) '
(today**.) '
() '
