(development, AI infrastructure, recommendation engine, and security.* **Rs 12 lakh ) '
(Customer acquisition:** campus marketing, digital campaigns, and user acquisition.* **Rs) '
(8 lakh  Team:** product, engineering, growth, and nutrition expertise.* **Rs 7 lakh ) '
(Partnerships & operations:** food/grocery partnerships, nutrition content, and) '
(operational costs.* **Rs 5 lakh  Legal, compliance & contingency.**The investor gets) '
(**10% ownership in FitBite**, so their return comes from the value of that equity rather) '
(than a guaranteed repayment.Our goal is to use this capital to reach strong) '
(product-market fit, grow our paying user base, establish recurring subscription revenue,) '
(and build strategic partnerships. If FitBite grows significantly, the investor's 10%) '
(stake becomes more valuable. A future acquisition, secondary sale, or larger funding) '
(round could provide a potential liquidity event.For example, if FitBite eventually) '
(reaches a **Rs 50 crore valuation**, the investor's 10% stake would be worth) '
